.TH OBS-LIVESTREAM 1 "October 2026" "just3ws" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obs-livestream \- manage, validate, and broadcast UGtastic oral history rewatch livestreams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bundle exec rake validate:obs
.br
.B ruby bin/validate_obs_setup.rb
[\fB\-\-live\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/install-obs-config.sh
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/update-overlay-state.sh
[\fB\-\-episode\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-guest\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-conference\fR \fICONF\fR] [\fB\-\-prompt\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/test-audio-routing.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B obs-livestream
is the automation and configuration suite for the "The Sound Above" oral history rewatch stream. Hosted by Mike Hall (Software Craftsmanship Signatory #106), the series reviews over 200 UGtastic interviews (2010\[en]2015), early Chicago software craftsmanship history, and the evolution of developer identity as the industry transitions into the AI era.
.PP
The toolchain provides declarative OBS Studio 32 scene collections, Apple Silicon M4 hardware-accelerated encoding profiles, native macOS Golden Gate digital sound capture, interactive HTML/CSS/JS browser overlays, and automated contract testing.
.SH PRODUCTION SCENES
The scene collection defines eight purpose-built broadcast scenes:
.TP
.B 01. Starting Soon
Ambient slate title screen with live episode card, quote carousel, and animated pulse indicator.
.TP
.B 02. Monologue / Full Camera
Full-screen host camera with lower-third HUD for framing historical context and opening thesis.
.TP
.B 03. Reaction \- Video Focus
Large-format Orion browser window capture (80% canvas) paired with host camera picture-in-picture in the lower right, Now Watching HUD, and isolated application audio.
.TP
.B 04. Split Screen \- Video & Research
Side-by-side comparison: Orion video playback on the left, secondary research browser or terminal on the right showing transcripts or timeline data on just3ws.localhost.
.TP
.B 05. Workbench \- Code & Terminal
Full-screen terminal window capture (18pt font minimum) with host camera inset for code analysis, git archaeology, and zdots platform tooling demonstrations.
.TP
.B 06. Guest & Co-Host Discussion
Two-up side-by-side camera boxes with shared screen inset for retrospective discussions with community veterans.
.TP
.B 07. Intermission / BRB
Standby card ("Holding the Thread") displaying the active topic while stepping away from the workbench.
.TP
.B 08. Outro & Next Stream
Closing credits, archive resource links, and next episode preview.
.SH AUDIO ARCHITECTURE (MACOS GOLDEN GATE)
OBS on macOS Golden Gate (Darwin 27) utilizes native ScreenCaptureKit and CoreAudio capture:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Per-Application Audio (\fIsck_audio_capture\fR):
Taps the digital PCM stream of the Orion browser directly. Completely isolates video playback while automatically filtering out Mail chimes, Slack dings, terminal bells, and Spotify.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Desktop Audio (\fIcoreaudio_output_capture\fR):
Taps default system output at a locked 48,000 Hz sample rate without requiring third-party virtual audio loopback drivers (Soundflower and BlackHole are obsolete).
.IP \(bu 2
.B 4-Track Master Recording:
Advanced recording captures four independent, synchronized audio tracks simultaneously into hybrid MOV containers: Track 1 (Composite Stream Mix), Track 2 (Host Mic Isolated), Track 3 (Orion Video Isolated), Track 4 (Guest Isolated).
.SH OVERLAYS
Browser overlays in \fIobs/overlays/\fR poll \fIobs/overlays/overlay-state.json\fR every 2.5 seconds:
.TP
.B lower-third.html
Renders interviewee name, event, year, role, and the central Sound Above philosophical prompt.
.TP
.B now-watching.html
Renders floating metadata card with recording indicator, era pill, and episode topic.
.TP
.B stream-starting.html
Pre-stream title card with animated pulse and rotating quotes from craftsmanship literature.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I obs/scenes/ugtastic-sound-above.json
Declarative OBS Studio 32 scene collection.
.TP
.I obs/profiles/The Sound Above/basic.ini
Hardware-tuned OBS profile for Apple Silicon M4.
.TP
.I obs/overlays/overlay-state.json
Live state synchronized to browser sources.
.TP
.I obs/curation/sequence-manifest.json
21-episode master curation sequence.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/obs-studio/
Installed OBS Studio configuration target.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Validate all OBS contracts and macOS environment:
bundle exec rake validate:obs

# Probe running OBS instance and WebSocket socket:
ruby bin/validate_obs_setup.rb --live

# Cue Episode 1 (Sergio Pereira):
./obs/scripts/update-overlay-state.sh --episode 1

# Synchronize repo configuration to OBS Studio:
./obs/scripts/install-obs-config.sh

# Run audio diagnostic and sample rate check:
./obs/scripts/test-audio-routing.sh
.fi
